// # Install Subsystem — Anchor for Agents
//
// Logline: How the toolchain lands on a machine. Bash bootstrap for curl | bash portability,
//          plus openOODA harness_wire.oo for cap-closed mcp/lsp/blackbox wiring.
//
// Setup: Pure structural file. VERSION must match the current git tag (RULES.oot §1.24 exception).
//
// Beats:
//   1. install.sh is the thin bash bootstrap (OS/arch, curl, std clone, shell rc). SHA-256 sidecar required; missing or mismatch refuses. VERSION must match the current git tag (RULES.oot §1.24 exception — install is hand-bumped because curl|bash has no git history at install time).
//   2. harness_wire.oo is the openOODA cap-closed wire (FsReadCap/FsWriteCap/EnvCap/ProcessCap, ≤256 lines per file)
//   3. Detects 20 harnesses (antigravity-cli, opencode, muse, grok, gemini, claude-code, claude-desktop, cursor, windsurf, codex, cline, continue, zed, vscode, goose, mistral-vibe, grok-build, mcode, devin, charm) and wires 18 via bash install.sh plus 12 via cap-closed harness_wire.oo (8 file merges + 4 ProcessCap CLI stubs) when ooda+oodac are installed. devin and charm are detected but not yet wired (see M1 in 2026-09-10 focused audit).
//   4. Idempotent, DRY_RUN preview, *.bak.openooda backup, y/n gated in install.sh, restart reminder
//   5. To propose a change, keep every .oo ≤256 lines and fail closed. No python fallback in .oo path.
//   6. Hybrid wiring: install.sh runs bash+python3 heredoc merges for 18 harnesses (the curl|bash default path). If ooda+oodac are on PATH, install.sh also runs harness_wire.oo for 8 file-merge harnesses (silent unless OPENOODA_DEBUG=1); on failure, falls back to bash. The .oo path is never the only path.

// harness_wire.oo is the cap-closed wire — see beats above (no import needed for structural anchor)
